    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Published results</h2>

      <p>
        The reported average Random Forest performance was:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Accuracy: 72%</li>
        <li>Precision: 71%</li>
        <li>Recall: 85%</li>
        <li>F1 score: 76%</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Random Forest feature importance and permutation importance both
        identified Sleep Stage 1 and Sleep Stage 3-4 as the most influential
        stage-level features. The result suggests that graph-based
        physiological connectivity during light and deeper sleep contains
        information relevant to differentiating the two study groups.
      </p>
    </section>

