    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Reproducible research software</h2>

      <p>
        The public repository contains the preserved publication-era scripts,
        a reusable Python package, command-line interfaces, historical
        configurations, automated tests, continuous-integration validation,
        machine-readable publication results, and a complete synthetic PSG
        demonstration.
      </p>

      <p>
        The original participant-level PSG recordings are protected clinical
        data and are not publicly distributed. The synthetic demonstration is
        provided only to validate that the software runs end to end. Synthetic
        metrics and feature importances have no clinical or publication-level
        interpretation.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Interpretation and limitations</h2>

      <p>
        The study used a limited cohort and should not be interpreted as a
        general-purpose clinical diagnostic system. The repository also
        documents historical methodological choices, including batch-level
        stage imputation, sign-inversion augmentation before cross-validation,
        direct use of correlation values as shortest-path weights, and
        unseeded stochastic components.
      </p>

      <p>
        These behaviors are preserved for scientific provenance rather than
        silently replaced. The reported metrics are maintained as the
        publication record and are not presented as deterministic
        regenerations from the public synthetic data.
      </p>
    </section>

